  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Velumeth~, Chief Fire Keeper
    
    Chief Fire Keeper of Nightfall Shelf. Velumeth~ is known almost exclusively for his role as appointed prosecutor in the Shadow Parliament's tribunal against the Midnight Claws, the covert organization led by Shadow-Broker Nyla that controlled fire-core distribution outside sanctioned channels for thirty winters.
    
    Velumeth~ presented the case under *Iudicium∴culum*. His central exhibit was a fire-core shipping ledger bound in treated seal-skin — its cipher broken only after Nyla's confession before the Aurora Stack council — documenting eleven hundred diverted fire-cores routed through Claws-controlled tunnels beyond any oversight the Flipper Accord provided. He produced a hand-drawn map of the Glow-Fissure's upper reaches that stopped at the third descent level, arguing the Claws had maintained a monopoly on the corruption site rather than containing it. He named the cartographer Kess, who had attempted a full Fissure survey and returned speaking in phonemes her own colony-mates could not parse before disappearing from the Shelf entirely.
    
    His prosecution's defining argument reframed the Claws not as thieves but as **architects of dependency**: settlements receiving Claws fire-cores during shortages learned official channels could not be trusted, because the Claws had already bled those channels dry. Presiding Chair Umbraae~ dissolved the organization and sentenced surviving members to supervised labor-service above the third descent level.
    
    Velumeth~ carries a fire-core rod and favors ash-gray formal wrappings. Beyond the tribunal, the record is silent.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771593367987_0", anchor: "its cipher broken only after Nyla's confession before the Aurora Stack council", text: "Then what was Velumeth~ prosecuting *with* before the cipher broke? He had a sealed ledger he could not read, a map that stopped where the interesting territory began, and a missing cartographer. Nyla confessed to Aurora — not to the Nightshelf, not to the tribunal — and only then did the ledger become legible. This is not a prosecution that produced a conviction. This is a confession that produced a prosecution. Velumeth~ was staging the formalities around a verdict Nyla had already delivered to a foreign body. Every procedural flourish in this entry — *Iudicium∴culum*, the central exhibit, the defining argument — is scenery.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593367987_1", anchor: "eleven hundred diverted fire-cores", text: "Eleven hundred. Thirty winters. From a forensic accounting of a cipher ledger covering three decades of covert distribution through unmapped tunnels. Not eleven hundred and six. Not twenty-eight winters. The round numbers tell me someone decided what the figure should feel like rather than what it was.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593367987_2", anchor: "Beyond the tribunal, the record is silent", text: "Chief Fire Keeper is not an entry-level appointment. A penguin holding that title has a career before and after any single tribunal, or the title is ceremonial and the prosecution was handed to someone expendable. Either way this silence is not absence — it is the Nightshelf filing system doing what it does. Somewhere in ☽'shadow code there is a full dossier. The fact that I cannot read it does not make it empty.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
